          "id": 1640196740,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "At least in macOS, the problem is that, for whatever wacky reasons Apple has, double-clicking on the Wireshark icon in a directory containing a Wireshark app bundle causes it to launch in `/`, so that's the current working directory.",
